formed polluted Hamm Creek into a thriving salmon habitat]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132860645.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[John Beal, a dedicated Vietnam veteran, took it upon himself to revive Seattle's Hamm Creek, which had suffered from pollution. His approach included removing trash and reintroducing native plants to restore the ecosystem. By founding I'M A PAL, Beal rallied local volunteers and secured necessary funding, reigniting community passion. His perseverance has led to Hamm Creek's reintegration with the Duwamish River, fostering rich wildlife and ensuring a lasting ecological legacy.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/how-vietnam-veteran-john-beal-turned-seattles-polluted-hamm-creek-into-a-thriving-salmon-habitat-after-doctors-gave-him-just-four-months-to-live/articleshow/132860645.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/how-vietnam-veteran-john-beal-turned-seattles-polluted-hamm-creek-into-a-thriving-salmon-habitat-after-doctors-gave-him-just-four-months-to-live/articleshow/132860645.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-04T19:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132860645,imgsize-261841.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Hidden for 2,000 years, this Egyptian tomb held 560 ushabti figurines meant to serve the dead in the afterlife]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132860819.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Excavations at Tell Quesna have revealed a remarkable funerary complex adorned with hundreds of burial artifacts. Among the treasures, archaeologists discovered 560 ushabti figurines, believed to assist the deceased in the afterlife. Additional finds included protective amulets and pottery, with imported items from Rhodes highlighting trade links with the Mediterranean. These artifacts significantly enhance our knowledge of ancient Egyptian spiritual beliefs and rituals.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/hidden-for-2000-years-this-egyptian-tomb-held-560-ushabti-figurines-meant-to-serve-the-dead-in-the-afterlife/articleshow/132860819.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/hidden-for-2000-years-this-egyptian-tomb-held-560-ushabti-figurines-meant-to-serve-the-dead-in-the-afterlife/articleshow/132860819.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-04T19:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132860819,imgsize-127953.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Archaeologists uncover 600-year-old saint statue beneath Berlin's oldest district]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132861058.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Excavations in Berlin's Molkenmarkt uncovered medieval religious artefacts from the 14th and 15th centuries.  These discoveries include well-preserved saint figurines and a Madonna and Child sculpture.  An extraordinary cache of ceramic figures containing human bone fragments was also found.  These finds offer fresh evidence of devotional practices in medieval urban life.  The discoveries contribute to understanding medieval Berlin and its spiritual traditions.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/archaeologists-discover-a-rare-600-year-old-saint-statue-and-human-bone-reliquaries-beneath-berlins-oldest-neighbourhood/articleshow/132861058.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/archaeologists-discover-a-rare-600-year-old-saint-statue-and-human-bone-reliquaries-beneath-berlins-oldest-neighbourhood/articleshow/132861058.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-04T20:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132861058,imgsize-102046.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[When Jeff Bezos asked his team to help after a rainforest charity saving the Amazon said it was blocked from using 'Amazon' in Google Ads]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132863556.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/when-jeff-bezos-asked-his-team-to-help-after-a-rainforest-charity-saving-the-amazon-said-it-was-blocked-from-using-amazon-in-google-ads/articleshow/132863556.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/when-jeff-bezos-asked-his-team-to-help-after-a-rainforest-charity-saving-the-amazon-said-it-was-blocked-from-using-amazon-in-google-ads/articleshow/132863556.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-04T19:29:34+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132863576,imgsize-471229.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Only 4 companies? Critics say barring small companies from hiring H-1B for 1-2 years is not enough]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132861869.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/only-4-companies-critics-say-barring-small-companies-from-hiring-h-1b-for-1-2-years-is-not-enough/articleshow/132861869.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/only-4-companies-critics-say-barring-small-companies-from-hiring-h-1b-for-1-2-years-is-not-enough/articleshow/132861869.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-04T18:36:14+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132861967,imgsize-34540.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists discover Greenland sharks can see for centuries, debunking blindness myth]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132859680.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Recent studies reveal that Greenland sharks possess well-preserved visual systems that can last for centuries, challenging the previous notion that they were nearly blind. Research shows that their eyes are uniquely suited for low-light environments, demonstrating impressive adaptability. Scientists found healthy rod cells and active genes responsible for light detection, indicating these sharks have a remarkable ability to maintain their eyesight throughout their extended lifespans.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-discover-greenland-sharks-can-survive-for-centuries-with-functioning-eyesight-overturning-the-long-held-belief-that-they-are-blind/articleshow/132859680.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-discover-greenland-sharks-can-survive-for-centuries-with-functioning-eyesight-overturning-the-long-held-belief-that-they-are-blind/articleshow/132859680.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-04T18:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132859680,imgsize-119413.cms"/></item></channel></rss>